{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_pspl_model", "label": "PSPL (Paczynski point-source point-lens) model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Two datasets, two different pipelines", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_2l1s_model", "label": "2L1S (point-source binary-lens) model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "O-03-BLG235's PSPL-vs-2L1S model comparison", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_annual_parallax", "label": "Annual parallax (Gould 2004 geocentric formalism)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Annual parallax + robust (Student-t) likelihood for PSPL fits", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_studentt_likelihood", "label": "Student-t robust likelihood", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Annual parallax + robust (Student-t) likelihood for PSPL fits", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chosen over Huber/sigma-clipping because a residual diagnostic on O-05-BLG086 showed a globally heavier-than-Gaussian error distribution (excess kurtosis 1.23, dof~6 MLE) rather than a small population of discrete outliers -- a smooth down-weight fits the observed error shape better than a hard/linear cutoff."}, {"id": "claude_huber_loss", "label": "Huber loss likelihood (2L1S track)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Session 11 (2L1S PSPL-vs-2L1S section)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tried as the first well-documented alternative to Student-t for the 2L1S track's caustic-spike problem, with DELTA=1.345 fixed (not fit) so it needs no normalizing-constant correction; ultimately found (with chi2 and Student-t) to fail to fit the caustic spike at all, so parked rather than pursued further."}, {"id": "claude_flux_calibration_pipeline", "label": "O-03-BLG235 calibrate-once-then-fit pipeline", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "O-03-BLG235's calibrate-once-then-fit pipeline", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "OGLE and MOA report incompatible units with no valid direct conversion, so a single shared-trajectory fit (fit_joint_pspl) is run once to solve fs_ogle/fb_ogle/fs_moa, then both instruments are inverted onto a common magnification scale A(t). This freezes the flux calibration at a point estimate, which session 5/6 showed can be measurably biased (chi2 31,982 vs 1,953) for a real caustic-crossing trajectory not seen during calibration."}, {"id": "claude_near_miss_cusp_problem", "label": "Near-miss-cusp search-landscape problem", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "O-03-BLG235's PSPL-vs-2L1S model comparison (in progress)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Under the fixed-then-fixed flux calibration, multi-start and most MCMC 2L1S searches converge to non-physical trajectories that never cross the caustic (no 3->5 image-count transition) yet score numerically better on chi2/Student-t/Huber than Bond et al.'s own published, genuinely-crossing solution -- only catchable via the image-count invariant check, not from the loss value alone. Session 11 found all three tried likelihoods disagree with each other on fitted parameters far more than a likelihood-shape difference should cause, pointing at this search-landscape issue as the dominant open problem rather than loss-function choice."}, {"id": "claude_output_layout", "label": "Output layout convention (scratch/ vs. pipeline dirs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Output layout", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_shared_helpers", "label": "Shared plotting/MCMC helpers convention", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Shared plotting/MCMC helpers -- do not re-copy these", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_rules", "label": "Repository rules section", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "## Rules", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_instructions", "label": "Repository instructions section", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "## Instructions", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_collaboration_mode", "label": "User-writes/Claude-reviews collaboration mode", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Rule 6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Default mode: Claude gives direction/hints and lets the user write the implementation, then simplifies with ponytail afterward. Explicitly and deliberately overridden several times (sessions 3, 5, 9) for specific pieces where Claude implemented directly instead, each logged as a scoped, one-off exception rather than a standing change."}, {"id": "claude_grill_me_consensus", "label": "/grill-me consensus mechanism", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "## Instructions, item 3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Used to reach consensus before acting on any new want not already in CHANGELOG.md, and to confirm next-session goals during 'save state'. Session 11 found diminishing returns in running further grill-me rounds once real run results already answered the practical question -- a direct decision from someone who saw the results was judged faster and no less valid."}, {"id": "claude_graphify", "label": "/graphify knowledge-graph skill", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "## Instructions, item 2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_lc_models_trajectory", "label": "lc_models.trajectory()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Two datasets, two different pipelines", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_lc_models_magnification", "label": "lc_models.magnification()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Two datasets, two different pipelines", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_lc_models_flux", "label": "lc_models.flux()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Two datasets, two different pipelines", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_lc_models_magnitude", "label": "lc_models.magnitude()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Two datasets, two different pipelines", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_lc_models_binary_trajectory", "label": "lc_models.binary_trajectory()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "O-03-BLG235's PSPL-vs-2L1S model comparison", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_lc_models_binary_magnification", "label": "lc_models.binary_magnification()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "O-03-BLG235's PSPL-vs-2L1S model comparison", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claude_lc_models_sun_earth_projection", "label": "lc_models.sun_earth_projectio